FRACTINT(1)

NAME
    fractint - run upstream Fractint/Xfractint on the framebuffer

SYNOPSIS
    fractint [fractint-options]

DESCRIPTION
    Starts the SmallOS port of upstream Xfractint 20.04p16.  The port uses the
    SmallOS framebuffer as a 1024x768 indexed 256-color video mode and ships
    the generated Fractint help database in /usr/share/xfractint/fractint.hlp.

    With no options, SmallOS supplies a default Mandelbrot command line:
    video=F2 type=mandel passes=1 maxiter=150 inside=0.

EXAMPLES
    Fractint options are the upstream options, for example:

        fractint type=newton maxiter=80
        fractint type=complexnewton maxiter=80
        fractint type=julia params=-0.74543,0.11301

FILES
    /usr/share/xfractint/fractint.hlp
        Generated upstream help database.

    /usr/share/xfractint
        Fractint data directory.  The image stages the help database,
        sstools.ini, and upstream maps, parameter sets, formulas, L-system
        definitions, and IFS definitions both at the search root and in
        canonical upstream subdirectories.

KEYS
    Fractint keeps its classic keyboard interface.  Press Q to leave the
    framebuffer view in the SmallOS port.  Menus and type-specific prompts use
    the normal Fractint keyboard flow.

NOTES
    SmallOS keeps Fractint's normal renderers.  The experimental adaptive
    triangle renderer was removed; use the standard Fractint pass modes.
    Keyboard controls are decoded through the shared term_keys runtime helper,
    not a Fractint-private escape-sequence parser.

    Fractint still owns its 256-entry palette.  The SmallOS adapter, kept
    outside the vendored tree under src/user/ports/fractint, feeds that
    palette into the shared gfx_indexed layer, which maintains the indexed
    shadow pixel plane, converts values to XRGB8888, batches dirty
    presentation, and recolors the framebuffer when the palette changes.
    Menu cells use the shared gfx_text renderer.

SEE ALSO
    mandel(1), plasma(1), bmpview(1), smallos(7)
